{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Completed outcome\n\nMerged commit `586357b70996537ac790a82da56fe6e372d0d3e5` implements a rollback-safe,\ndurable bridge pause/resume surface while preserving old readers, old reconcile vocabulary, and\nexisting workflow/environment behavior.\n\nThe remote `refs/reconciler/gate` blob remains dual-format:\n`gated_mode: \"reconcile-check\"` plus `paused`, `reason`, `who`, and `paused_at`.\nPause provenance uses repository `git user.email` and first-pause UTC RFC3339 time. Same-reason\npause is idempotent and preserves metadata; different reason, blank reason, missing identity,\nmissing remote, and CAS movement refuse without overwrite. Resume deletes only the observed ref\nOID and can recover a corrupt blob without decoding it.\n\nA new pause blocks before pass-lock acquisition or ticket mutation and returns rc 0 with one exact,\nanchored, JSON-decoded `BRIDGE_PAUSED:` line. The scheduled workflow recognizes only that complete\nrc-0 marker and skips commit-and-push. Ordinary rc 0, malformed/unanchored markers, corrupt rc 1,\nand legacy gate rc 4 retain their existing behavior. The pre-gate `reconcile-check` early return\nand old `rebar reconcile --mode` vocabulary remain functional.\n\n## Authoritative evidence\n\n- Gerrit 1549: `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, zero unresolved comments, merged as\n  `586357b709`; retry CI run 31272528686 completed 15/15 jobs successfully.\n- Held-out affected oracle: 82/82 green. Final pre-push affected/module-size oracle: 86/86 green.\n- Static gates: lint, Ruff format, actionlint, complexity, typecheck, config-check, generated CLI\n  reference, module-size, and diff checks green.\n- Mutation teeth: tests went RED when additive `gated_mode` was removed, marker anchoring was\n  weakened, and corrupt-gate traceback handling was regressed; production was restored after each.\n- Primary contract tests:\n  `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py`,\n  `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py`,\n  `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock_ref_backend.py`,\n  `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py`, and\n  `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py`.\n- Implementation/docs:\n  `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py`,\n  `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py`,\n  `_advisory_lock.py`, `__main__.py`,\n  `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`, CLI help/reference, user guide, exit codes, and release\n  notes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The durable operator contract is complete and rollback-safe: every pause blob retains\n      `gated_mode: reconcile-check` plus `paused/reason/who/paused_at`; the pre-change decoder\n      accepts it; repository git email and first-pause RFC3339 provenance are enforced; blank,\n      missing-identity, missing-remote, different-reason, and CAS-conflict cases refuse without\n      overwrite; same-reason pause is metadata-stable; resume is observed-OID CAS and clears absent,\n      valid, or corrupt state safely. Proof:\n      `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py`,\n      `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py`, and\n      `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock_ref_backend.py`.\n- [x] Runtime and workflow behavior is complete without regressions: pause and corrupt-gate paths\n      return before lock/pass/ticket mutation; pause emits only the exact anchored four-key rc-0\n      `BRIDGE_PAUSED` line and skips scheduled commit-and-push; corrupt state emits the exact rc-1\n      recovery line without traceback and is repaired by resume; ordinary success, malformed or\n      unanchored markers, legacy gate rc 4, benign/generic mappings, old `rebar reconcile --mode`,\n      and the pre-gate `reconcile-check` return remain functional. Proof:\n      `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`,\n      `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`,\n      `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py`,\n      `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py`, and\n      `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py`.\n- [x] The staged public contract and exclusions are complete: CLI help, generated reference, user\n      guide, exit-code docs, and release notes expose `preview/sync/pause/resume`; no `--until`,\n      automatic expiry, new-only blob, gate rename, or old-vocabulary removal shipped. Proof:\n      `src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge.txt`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt`,\n      `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md`,\n      `docs/release-notes.md`, and `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py`.\n\n## Residual disposition\n\nMCP and library pause/resume parity is filed in existing dependent story\n`f789-3f9d-8b35-4e0d`. Near-cap `_ref_lock.py` restructuring remains owned by\n`5e53-234f-5c65-477d` and is linked to this story. No test exclusion or weaker validation remains.\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786217441540310001,"uuid":"851582ed-269d-444a-add1-41398fbb653d"}